      "writtenOn": "2024-11-05T23:57:06Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I think you can change to the shell UID by using the version of runAsShell (or adoptShellPermissionIdentity) that does not take permissions strings. There are reasons not to do this though -for example, if anything else in the test is running, then it will lose the permissions it previously had when you do this.\n\nBut there are other ways of doing this. For example, we have other tests that use multiple UIDs such as CtsHostsideNetworkTests. It should be fairly easy to add a test there.",
